libva-v4l2_request (sofus13 1.3): keep frames visible to clients that hold
exported surfaces (fixes green video in Chromium/Helium on Apple AVD).

1. Chromium exports every VA surface once, before its first decode, and then
   displays that dma-buf. The driver handed out zeroed standalone backing for
   the unbound surface and dropped it on first bind, decoding into a separate
   CAPTURE buffer, so Chromium only ever showed zeros (green). Backing that was
   really exported is now kept and each decode is copied into it at
   vaEndPicture() (synchronously, with dma-buf cache sync).

2. vaDestroyContext() freed every CAPTURE buffer, so surfaces the client still
   held (end of stream, resolution change) lost their pixels. Decodes are now
   finished and the buffer's dma-buf is handed over to the surface first.

--- a/src/context.c
+++ b/src/context.c
@@ -335,6 +335,65 @@
